<BaseLayout title="About — Doan Van Tai" description="A little more about Doan Van Tai, a Computer Networks student at UIT working toward a career as a Research Engineer.">
  <div class="container page-header"><a class="breadcrumb" href="/">← Home</a><p class="eyebrow">A LITTLE MORE ABOUT ME</p><h1>Curiosity, with a<br />practical side.</h1></div>
  <div class="container page-body about-page-grid"><article class="prose"><p>{profile.bio}</p><p>My Vietnamese name is <strong>Đoàn Văn Tài</strong>. I’m based in Ho Chi Minh City, Vietnam, and expect to complete my Bachelor of Engineering in Computer Networks and Communications in 2027.</p><h2>What I’m working toward</h2><p>I want to develop as a Research Engineer: someone who can engage with a research question, turn it into a working implementation, and evaluate the result carefully. In the longer term, I’m interested in pursuing graduate research in networks and intelligent systems.</p><h2>What draws my attention</h2><p>Network Digital Twins, network optimization, and AI / ML for networking are the core of my current work. I’m particularly interested in what happens when the information available to a decision-maker is stale, incomplete, or imperfectly modeled.</p><p>That interest connects the systems side of my work—SDN testbeds, synchronization, and cloud infrastructure—with questions about uncertainty, routing, and decision quality.</p><h2>How I approach a project</h2><ul><li><strong>Start with a concrete question.</strong> Decide what the system or experiment should help us understand.</li><li><strong>Build something inspectable.</strong> Keep the implementation, assumptions, and evaluation connected.</li><li><strong>Keep the limits visible.</strong> A working pipeline is a useful starting point; it is not, by itself, evidence that a hypothesis is true.</li></ul><h2>Education</h2><p><strong>University of Information Technology, VNU-HCM</strong><br/>B.Eng. Computer Networks and Communications<br/>2023–2027 (expected) · GPA 3.52 / 4.00</p><h2>Technical toolkit</h2><div class="skills-grid">{profile.skills.map(skill=><div class="skill-group"><h3>{skill.title}</h3><p>{skill.items}</p></div>)}</div><h2>Let’s connect</h2><p>I’m open to Research Intern, Research Assistant, and R&D opportunities, especially where networking, digital twins, and machine learning meet.</p><p><a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a> · <a href={profile.github}>GitHub</a></p><a class="text-link" href="/cv/">View my CV <Icon size={15}/></a></article><figure class="about-page-photo"><img src="/images/tai-sunset.jpg" alt="Doan Van Tai at the seaside beneath a pink sunset" width="1368" height="1824"/><figcaption>A little perspective beyond the screen.</figcaption></figure></div>
</BaseLayout>
